WEBVTT

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:02.850
The Var syndrome.

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:06.360
It suddenly subverts a person's mind and rouses them into a frenzy.

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:11.690
People face this terrible threat all around the galaxy.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:19.330
To combat this, the tactical sound unit Walkure was assembled.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:27.430
Their singing is capable of appeasing those under the effects of Var.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:43.080
I'll show them the depth of our grudge!

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:47.410
I'll crush the earthlings, and Walkure with them!

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:49.610
Restrain yourself, Bogue.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.030
Master Hermann!

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:55.330
Please. I'm not your master anymore.

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:04.360
Our spread wings have become the song of the wind.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:17.330
Wonderful.

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:19.620
The relics are resonating stronger than ever.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.300
Your Highness!

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:36.360
Keith, my brother!

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.040
May the might of the winds flow beneath our wings.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.250
We need your song of the wind, Your Highness.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:56.040
<i>We've only got one shot at love,</i>

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:58.900
<i>so let's have fun inside of you</i>

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:02.760
<i>Let's share a selfish kiss</i>

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:13.560
<i>The petals of this flower fall in the wind</i>

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:19.030
<i>The stars are more than I could count</i>

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:22.570
<i>It doesn't matter if I blame it all on you,</i>

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:25.320
<i>swallowing back my tears</i>

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:30.160
<i>I can't tell anyone about how my heart races</i>

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.370
<i>Reach out</i>

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.710
<i>Until it all breaks apart</i>

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.620
<i>Reach out</i>

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:36.850
<i>Until you can take flight</i>

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:38.340
<i>To the ends</i>

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:39.170
<i>Deep in my heart</i>

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.960
<i>Of time</i>

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:41.760
<i>There is a prayer</i>

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.680
<i>Just feel, just believe</i>

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:48.780
<i>and speed through it all</i>

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:51.930
<i>We've only got one shot at love,</i>

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:54.690
<i>so let's have fun inside of you</i>

00:02:54.690 --> 00:03:00.270
<i>Let's share a kiss faster than light, just wait for me</i>

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:02.900
<i>My body almost forgot</i>

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:05.910
<i>My heart kept beating loudly</i>

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:11.340
<i>Escape your chains, they're all but a dream</i>

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:18.050
<i>Tear them off and come at me, just like that</i>

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:26.490
The rising star of Walkure: Freyja Wion!

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:28.510
She will be making her debut tomorrow

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:32.010
in the unit's Waccine show on planet Randor.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.310
She will join the team's ace, Mikumo Guyne—

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:42.030
Looking back at when I was asked to take part in the genesis of Walkure—

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.870
Thank you!

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:46.820
And a hip, hip, hurrah for Fre-Fre 
and Haya-Haya's big debuts!

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:47.950
Cheers!

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:50.250
Welcome to Chaos!

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:51.210
Welcome!

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:53.540
Cheers.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:58.680
I, Freyja Wion, will devote my life to Walkure!

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.470
She always overdoes it...

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:05.810
And now, a few words from our rookie!

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:07.330
Like, right now?

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:10.560
Don't be shy. Just say hi!

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:13.060
Sign: Freyja's (and Hayate's) Super Welcome Party

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.480
Next course!

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:21.950
A Ragnyannyan specialty:

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:23.780
Fried fermented spiders!

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:30.720
Hey, Messer,

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:34.960
is it true that Waccine shows prevent any further appearance of Var in the area?

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.750
You bet it is!

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:42.010
The songs of Walkure can not only 
suppress, but also prevent the Var!

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.580
You're very knowledgeable, Zack.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:45.180
Place and time, boy.

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:47.600
A Waccine show?

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.310
The government of Randor requested it.

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:54.440
They say the risk of a Var breakout has been on the rise.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:57.560
Does it have to be live?

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.940
Why not use pre-recorded songs?

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:04.380
When we sing, we generate biological fold waves which calm down the Var.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:10.030
If it's recorded or digitized, the 
effects are practically erased.

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:14.710
Live is best.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.890
Are you gonna sing too, Hayate?

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:17.540
No.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.480
We'll be doing an air show.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:25.340
There is a chance that those unknowns will show up again.

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:28.390
Don't let your guard down and follow my orders.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.300
Indeed, indeed.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:35.240
Are you making fun of me?

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:36.730
I'd never!

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:39.720
What did Lady M say?

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:44.350
We don't have time to wait for
 Freyja's abilities to stabilize.

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:45.880
We're always out of time.

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:48.500
Have you told her about fold receptors?

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:51.240
Not yet. Does Hayate know?

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:52.660
I haven't said anything.

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:55.280
The mood's perfect.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:57.160
They should just start dating.

00:05:57.860 --> 00:05:59.480
Are you going back?

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:01.340
It doesn't hurt to kick back once in a while.

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:04.010
I'll be on standby at the base.

00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:05.660
I see.

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:06.970
Thanks!

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:14.240
My stomach is about to asplode.

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.920
Here. You ate too much.

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.520
Fank you...

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:22.940
Ap'ju!

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:24.790
Come on, say it right.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:26.680
Have you gotten used to Ragna yet?

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:27.450
Indeed I have!

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:31.870
It's actually a lot like my hometown.

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:34.370
On Windermere?

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.180
The wind was so nice there.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:39.420
The sky and the land were both completely white.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:42.610
Covered in snow, and there was a bunch of orchards.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:45.570
Uh...

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:47.090
How is it similar to here?

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:50.400
Now that you mention it...

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:51.720
That's a good question!

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:56.370
Home, huh?

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:15.740
Why do people... Why do I sing?

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:23.170
Aether, separation complete. Gravity controls nominal.

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:25.890
Releasing fold energy from condensers.

00:07:25.890 --> 00:07:30.360
Aether, switching to interstellar cruise mode.

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:33.940
Onboard gravity control to mode C. Connecting heat pile clusters.

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:35.300
All nominal.

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:37.770
Initiating fold hop.

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:41.230
We are scheduled to de-fold in 30 minutes.

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:43.100
Is this her?

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:45.060
She's a looker!

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:48.030
The VF-31 Siegfried.

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:51.840
It's a bleeding edge fighter stock equipped with an inertial control system.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:54.170
Wasted on you, if you ask me.

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:57.320
Also,

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:00.620
we have a lil' onboarding gift for you.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:05.630
Hey-o! Haya-Haya, we know you hate the support AI,

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:09.700
so we tuned Siegy just for you!

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:13.550
This way you don't have to wear a helmet.

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:18.920
But if things go south, be sure to use the X-gear system, all right?

00:08:21.170 --> 00:08:22.530
Thanks a lot.

00:08:22.530 --> 00:08:24.230
Show us what you've got.

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:30.000
Hi, Freyja.

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:32.390
Hello!

00:08:32.390 --> 00:08:34.030
Hayate?

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:38.070
What's wrong? Got stage fright for your first show?

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:39.870
I'm...

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:45.040
You've had that on you at Al-Shahal too. Some sort of good luck charm?

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:47.770
Kinda.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:52.420
I got it from an earthling who visited Windermere when I was little.

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:55.670
This is how I learned about the music from outside.

00:08:58.020 --> 00:08:59.960
Lynn Minmay.

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:02.340
The Fire Bomber.

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:04.500
Sheryl Nome.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:06.080
Ranka Lee.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:08.570
And finally Walkure.

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:12.060
I thought they were so cool.

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:14.550
I wanted to be just like them.

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:16.480
But...

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:18.490
That's not like you.

00:09:19.310 --> 00:09:21.740
If you're willing to risk your life, you can fly.

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:22.900
Did you forget?

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:27.880
You're right.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:29.790
If I try, I can fly!

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:31.840
Life's but 30 years!

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:34.800
If I've got time to worry, I've got time to fly!

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:38.170
Thanks, Haya-Haya!

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:42.200
Don't call me that.

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:48.620
Windermereans die young in exchange for their extreme physical abilities.

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:50.900
Their average life span is about 30 years.

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:55.150
Feels unreal when I look at her.

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:06.620
Planet Randor

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:08.670
Freyja!

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:10.200
Y-Yes?

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:12.380
What are you going to sing for?

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:14.910
Um...

00:10:14.910 --> 00:10:17.510
What about you, Kumokumo?

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:19.500
Well...

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:23.600
I'll tell you if you satisfy me tonight.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:26.940
If you can't, Walkure won't be needing you anymore.

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:33.270
That's enough talking.

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:35.400
Are we good to go?

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:39.860
For the galaxy...

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:41.040
For someone out there...

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:42.320
We will...

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:44.360
go all out...

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:46.330
and enjoy ourselves!

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:48.890
Go, Walkure!

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:55.300
<i>Welcome to Walkure World!</i>

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:11.650
This is the best feeling in the world!

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:16.690
Music is love!

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:20.400
Music is hope!

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:25.200
Music is life!

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:31.670
Music is mystery!

00:11:35.470 --> 00:11:40.090
If I try, I can fly... If I try, I can fly... 
If I try, I can fly... If I try...

00:11:41.110 --> 00:11:43.140
Yikes!

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:54.190
Music is energy!

00:11:55.850 --> 00:11:56.740
It's her!

00:11:56.740 --> 00:11:57.980
The new member!

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:05.680
She fell!

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:07.160
Look at that!

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:18.880
Lend an ear to the songs of a goddess!

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:22.300
Super Dimension Venus, Walkure!

00:12:24.490 --> 00:12:27.100
W-Walkure!

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:29.980
Walkure!

00:12:30.490 --> 00:12:33.690
Let's have an introduction from our newest member!

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:41.140
I'm Freyja Wion, 14, from Windermere, and I love apples.

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:43.910
N-Nice to eat you!

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:45.820
You the best!

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:47.530
My heart is yours!

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:51.160
Now, for our opening act,

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:53.660
Uncertain Cosmic Movement!

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:57.340
Fail, and you're fired.

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:08.300
<i>I don't care if I break the laws of physics</i>

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:12.810
<i>Just let me dance until I die! Ah!</i>

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:19.430
<i>Ride on! Three, two, one</i>

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:25.280
<i>Stars, people, and apples are all the same</i>

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:30.580
<i>We live in the same space, the same time</i>

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:39.920
<i>There might be laws, there may be rhythm</i>

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:48.260
<i>But if you break them, the pale blue sky will fall apart</i>

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:52.310
<i>Fall in love and you'll know</i>

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:56.080
<i>feelings rising like the wind</i>

00:13:56.080 --> 00:14:01.150
<i>The warmth around our touching hands</i>

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:03.440
<i>Dance, dance your dance</i>

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:06.780
<i>Our bodies pulse and awaken</i>

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:10.620
<i>in an uncertain cosmic movement</i>

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:11.870
Hayate!

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:17.410
<i>Your voice is the wave our love rides on</i>

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:14.580
Not following orders again...

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:19.880
<i>Just a little more, just an inch</i>

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:24.920
<i>Beyond this point we're free</i>

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:24.100
It's dancing!

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:28.180
<i>See, how a flash of a kiss</i>

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:33.170
<i>can conquer the world for good</i>

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:33.680
The Immelmann dance, huh?

00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:35.180
<i>Boom! Boom! Boom boom space</i>

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:36.330
Whoopsie!

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:38.090
You okay, newbie?

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:41.210
Var emergence risk down to 48.

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:42.190
<i>Are you okay? Yeah! Three, two, one</i>

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:46.490
Freyja's fold receptors are non-active.

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:49.610
<i>Ride on! Ride on! Cosmic...</i>

00:14:53.160 --> 00:15:00.580
<i>Our bodies are boiling with overflowing love</i>

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:59.360
To all units!

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:00.580
Spread your wings!

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:07.940
<i>Just let our lives shine twice as bright now</i>

00:15:00.860 --> 00:15:03.040
For the Great Wind.

00:15:03.490 --> 00:15:07.450
Aether to Delta 1. Unknowns have appeared in orbit.

00:15:07.450 --> 00:15:08.940
Atmospheric entry detected.

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:11.540
<i>Our bodies sing aloud</i>

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:09.810
Here they come.

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:15.560
<i>in an uncertain cosmic motion</i>

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:16.270
We know...

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:21.750
<i>Your voice is the wave our love rides</i>

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:17.980
your weak spot.

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:23.390
<i>Just a little—</i>

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:30.530
They've researched us well.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:34.180
The enemy's jamming disabled our fold wave ampli—

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:35.360
Missiles incoming!

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:36.840
Get down!

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:42.620
We have to protect the civilians and Walkure!

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:53.900
More enemies?

00:15:53.900 --> 00:15:55.970
No, it's the Spacy!

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:58.810
Yay, reinforcements!

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:12.350
What?

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:14.200
What's this?

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:25.870
I can hear a voice.

00:16:25.870 --> 00:16:28.050
Someone else is singing out there too.

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:33.200
Why are Spacy units attacking us?

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:33.930
Seriously?!

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:37.640
Are they affected by the Var?

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:39.210
Delta 3, check!

00:16:39.210 --> 00:16:40.530
Aye, sir!

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:46.230
They're at 93.5%!

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:47.690
They've been hit by the Var!

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:51.740
But the Var is attacking in formation? Impossible!

00:16:54.420 --> 00:16:55.410
Run!

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:01.740
We've got no choice.

00:17:01.740 --> 00:17:04.870
Prioritize the safety of civilians and Walkure!

00:17:05.060 --> 00:17:05.960
Roger!

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:10.640
We attack?

00:17:10.640 --> 00:17:11.920
They're allies!

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:14.330
They're not themselves!

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:15.760
So what?

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:19.480
That might've been true earlier, 
but they're our enemies now.

00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:22.770
Our job is to protect, even at the risk of our lives.

00:17:23.170 --> 00:17:26.170
Same goes for Spacy pilots.

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:28.350
They know what they've signed up for.

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:31.870
Just the wing.

00:17:33.080 --> 00:17:34.940
If I can hit just the wing...

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:36.740
Delta 4, bogey on your six!

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:40.490
Your back is wide open.

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:48.330
Delta 2!

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:51.010
You almost got taken down because you hesitated!

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:54.090
Damn you!

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:55.550
You're done.

00:17:55.780 --> 00:17:57.010
Lord Keith?

00:17:57.980 --> 00:17:58.970
I know you.

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:02.890
You were there on Al-Shahal.

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:10.060
That movement... Could it be...?

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:15.400
Crap!

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:18.070
Fly! Hurry!

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:22.390
Yikes!

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:29.680
You okay, Freyja?

